node_modules/
coverage/
.vitest-cache/
*.log
.pi/auto-resume.json
# Per-session plans, written by extensions/plan.ts as `.pi/plan/<session-id>.json`. They belong to a session, not to
# the repository - a session's own durability comes from Pi's session store and from the summary its compaction writes,
# not from git - and committing them would put one file per session into a public repo forever.
.pi/plan/
# The idle-compaction decision log (`.pi/idle-compaction/log.jsonl`): one line per compaction decision, including the
# decisions to do nothing. It is evidence about a session, not a repository artifact, and it grows on every idle run.
.pi/idle-compaction/
# Background job state written by extensions/background.ts (`.pi/background/<session-id>/`): a job belongs to the
# session that started it, and its output log is runtime evidence, not something to commit.
.pi/background/

# Pi session artifacts: uploads and images the agent was shown. They belong to the session, not
# to the repository, and `git add -A` will otherwise commit a screenshot of someone’s screen into a public repo -
# which is exactly what happened in cdfbaa5.
.slopyphus/
